        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-05T10:29:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In a certificate chain, each non-root certificate (cert\\_i) involves two keys:\n\n- Subject Public Key: This key ([subject public key]\\_i) is included as plaintext within the cert\\_i itself.\n- Authority Key: This key ([authority key]\\_i) is not explicitly present in the certificate but is used to generate the signature for cert\\_i.\n\nFor a certificate chain to be cryptographically valid, the following relationship must hold:\n\n[subject public key]\\_i \u003d [authority public key]\\_[i+1]\n\nso that the subject public key embedded in cert\\_i can be used to verify the signature of the subsequent certificate, cert\\_[i+1]. This is also shown in [2].\n\nIn the context of the DICE chain, I need to access the algorithm of the subject public key used in the leaf DICE certificate of the handover. This allows me to derive the next-stage authority key using the same algorithm, as shown in the diagram[1], to make the chain cryptographically valid.\n\n[1] https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/main/docs/pvm_dice_chain.md#pvm-dice-handover\n[2]https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_of_trust#/media/File:Chain_of_trust_v2.svg",
      "parentUuid": "ce8efc12_21ff59dc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 132,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "2ed9266d63ecef6060c6b3332680c7d47cac5e41",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
