      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why not check that cose_key.alg matches Some(Algorithm::Assigned(_)) in the constructor, allowing this to -\u003e Algorithm?\n\nDone\n\n\u003e Otherwise, I don\u0027t see the point of PublicKey\n\nThe `PublicKey` struct primarily serves as an intermediary structure to enhance code readability and clarity here. Conceptually, it makes sense for a payload to have an associated subject public key, and for that public key to have a specified algorithm. This creates a natural flow as line 131 above. \n\nIf we were to bypass the PublicKey, we would end up with a payload directly containing an algorithm, which is less intuitive.",
